    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high-upside production today, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (85.90) and **Andy Pages** (74.42), who benefit immensely from a favorable encounter with Sugano. Both outfielders carry massive scoring potential due to the combination of a high-ceiling park factor and a weak opposing starter (4.93 xERA), making them the unquestioned anchors of our daily rotation. **Drake Baldwin** also vaults into the elite tier at 71.20; his leadoff assignment against Ober provides a substantial +10% boost to his efficiency score, and his solid xwOBA suggests he is primed to capitalize on the +19% SP skill advantage. **Jacob Wilson** remains a strong start at 60.31; despite facing Wacha, Wilson\u2019s ability to drive runs from the #2 spot keeps his floor significantly higher than the rest of the infield corps.\n\nThe most difficult decision of the day involved our middle infield depth, specifically balancing the marginal scores of **Gunnar Henderson** (50.62) and **Miguel Vargas** (51.34). While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a tough southpaw in McClanahan\u2014resulting in a -15% penalty due to platoon dynamics\u2014his elite base projection keeps him in the starting lineup over deeper bench options like **Curtis Mead** or **Nasim Nunez**. Similarly, **Sam Antonacci** sits at the lower end of our starts (42.58), narrowly edging out candidates like **Josh Jung** and **Dominic Smith** due to his projected spot in the order. We are monitoring the status of **Wade Meckler** and **Luis Lara**, but neither provides a high enough efficiency score to displace our primary starters today. \n\nWe are flagging the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Andy Pages**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Jackson Merrill** as a primary risk; should their actual batting orders drop significantly, their scores will regress toward their base projections. Furthermore, while **Miguel Vargas** and **Coby Mayo** possess respectable scores, they face tough matchups against Imanaga and McClanahan, respectively. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remain on the IL, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos** are unavailable due to team scheduling, leaving our roster flexibility limited. We will keep a close eye on the wind reports in the late afternoon games, as any shift could further dampen the output for **Luis Robert Jr.**, who is currently managing a delicate -15% platoon penalty against Buehler.",
